01:38.520 --> 01:39.740
Ohzora prepares to shoot!

01:41.310 --> 01:44.860
The previous duel between me and Schneider has numbed my leg!

01:44.860 --> 01:45.860
What should I do?

01:46.100 --> 01:49.300
Always let your instinct guide you!

01:50.700 --> 01:51.780
What?

01:55.790 --> 01:57.900
Ohzora suddenly passes backwards to Hyuga!

01:57.900 --> 01:59.540
Please, Hyuga-kun!

01:59.540 --> 02:00.420
Yeah!

02:01.040 --> 02:02.580
Hyuga prepares to shoot!

02:02.580 --> 02:04.140
I won't let you score!

02:04.140 --> 02:06.180
Out of the way!

02:06.180 --> 02:08.540
Here's my Neo Tiger Shot!

02:16.530 --> 02:18.330
Goal!

02:18.330 --> 02:19.970
2-1!

02:19.970 --> 02:22.800
Japan finally turns the game around!

02:29.290 --> 02:31.460
Nice shot, Hyuga-kun!

02:35.700 --> 02:38.200
Nice assist, Tsubasa!

02:40.840 --> 02:43.180
This Japanese Junior Youth team is amazing!

02:45.290 --> 02:49.210
I'll make sure to get back this goal!

02:55.340 --> 03:00.500
<b>Shine in Glory, Japanese Team!</b>

02:55.340 --> 03:00.500
<b>Shine in Glory, Japanese Team!</b>

03:03.600 --> 03:08.330
Japan's leading by one goal, and there's only 15 minutes left of the second half.

03:08.330 --> 03:11.330
The Japanese team has accomplished something remarkable {Timing:  I attempted to deal with the three-liner that Ulquyorra mentioned in his QC report.  Please tweak my timing for this line and the next one as you see fit.}

03:11.330 --> 03:13.100
by taking the lead against the top-seeded Germans.

03:15.100 --> 03:19.980
Japan, a nation not known for winning at soccer, has not only qualified for the final,

03:19.980 --> 03:23.490
but is now dominating Germany, one of the top teams in the world!

03:23.490 --> 03:27.100
Ohzora Tsubasa is, without a doubt, the driving force behind it.

03:30.440 --> 03:34.610
Tsubasa, you've really grown.

03:39.460 --> 03:40.140
What?!

03:42.040 --> 03:48.450
You've become an excellent soccer player who truly loves the sport.

03:48.450 --> 03:53.140
Tsubasa, win this final and become the number one in the world!

03:53.140 --> 03:54.960
You can do it!

03:55.590 --> 03:58.070
The game resumes with Germany kicking off.

03:59.020 --> 04:00.020
Here we go!

04:02.940 --> 04:05.660
My leg's still numb after my collision with Ohzora.

04:06.740 --> 04:09.190
Schneider passes the ball to Schester at his right.

04:09.190 --> 04:10.160
My leg's still...

04:10.160 --> 04:13.230
Let us do this, Tsubasa! We'll take care of it!

04:13.230 --> 04:14.260
Ishizaki-kun!

04:14.900 --> 04:16.580
I'll defend the goal!

04:16.580 --> 04:19.220
Ishizaki and the rest of you, go forward and intercept the ball!

04:19.220 --> 04:21.110
Hang in there, Japan!

04:21.110 --> 04:25.900
The defense, led by the keeper, Wakabayashi, counters Germany's attack!

04:27.340 --> 04:29.970
Oh, it's a center! Kartz is getting in position to finish it.

04:29.970 --> 04:31.090
Like I'll let you!

04:32.700 --> 04:33.800
It's been cleared!

04:33.800 --> 04:36.380
Japan mobilizes to defend their goal!

04:35.150 --> 04:39.020
Bah. He ruined another opportunity for me.

04:39.020 --> 04:40.920
There's only ten minutes left of this game.

04:40.920 --> 04:42.840
Nice clearing, Misaki!

04:42.840 --> 04:44.020
Keep it up, defense!

04:45.250 --> 04:49.560
We can't score? We, the reigning European champions?

04:52.640 --> 04:54.790
It's not the strong who win.

04:55.500 --> 04:57.990
The ones who win are strong!

04:59.060 --> 05:00.460
Schneider!

05:01.000 --> 05:03.860
Miräus, pass me the ball!

05:04.400 --> 05:05.700
It's Germany's throw-in.

05:10.340 --> 05:12.300
Schneider dribbles with eagerness!

05:12.300 --> 05:13.860
Schneider!

05:15.130 --> 05:16.580
I won't lose!

05:19.300 --> 05:20.980
Schneider is in a shooting position!

05:21.770 --> 05:23.040
Take this!

05:23.040 --> 05:24.460
Fire...

05:24.460 --> 05:26.390
We'll be the winners!

05:27.380 --> 05:29.060
...Shot!

05:29.060 --> 05:30.060
I won't let it past!

05:35.460 --> 05:36.620
He caught it!

05:36.620 --> 05:37.980
Wakabayashi-kun!

05:38.380 --> 05:41.980
Wakabayashi's diving catch stopped Schneider's Fire Shot.

05:44.590 --> 05:46.240
Wakabayashi!

05:54.220 --> 05:55.340
Hyuga!

05:57.940 --> 05:59.260
Kartz steals the pass!

05:59.260 --> 06:00.980
Kartz!

06:00.980 --> 06:02.510
It's not over yet, Schneider!

06:02.510 --> 06:03.940
The attacking continues!

06:03.940 --> 06:06.780
Now it's time to show our spirit!

06:07.820 --> 06:10.690
Kartz is completely right! Everybody, follow him!

06:10.690 --> 06:11.410
Yeah!

06:11.410 --> 06:14.140
This time, Kartz leads the German attack.

06:13.140 --> 06:15.270
Germany got their fire back!

06:15.270 --> 06:16.870
Be careful, guys!

06:22.830 --> 06:26.500
Somehow Kartz dodges Sawada with ease. It's splendid dribbling!

06:27.160 --> 06:29.500
Kartz is serious, eh?

06:29.500 --> 06:31.260
You won't get through!

06:31.260 --> 06:33.980
I don't have time to play around with you guys.

06:34.410 --> 06:35.340
Schester!

06:35.940 --> 06:38.700
Kartz makes a long pass to the side.

06:38.700 --> 06:39.660
You won't get through!

06:39.660 --> 06:40.540
Here!

06:41.030 --> 06:42.740
Schester makes a direct pass!

06:42.740 --> 06:46.820
Mark Kartz! He's the key player of this attack!

06:46.820 --> 06:49.780
Bravo, Wakabayashi, but it's too late!

06:51.270 --> 06:53.180
Margas passes directly to Kartz!

06:53.180 --> 06:54.420
Stop him!

06:54.420 --> 06:55.180
Yeah!

06:57.160 --> 06:58.580
What? Kartz ignores the ball!

06:58.580 --> 06:59.380
What?!

06:59.380 --> 07:04.180
And here's Schneider! The Japanese defense was completely outsmarted!

07:04.180 --> 07:06.300
I'll let you finish this, Schneider!

07:06.300 --> 07:09.660
We'll defend German soccer's proud record!

07:10.900 --> 07:11.580
What?!

07:11.580 --> 07:12.340
Good!

07:19.500 --> 07:20.180
What?!

07:28.540 --> 07:30.900
Let's do it this time, Wakabayashi!

07:31.590 --> 07:32.880
With his left?

07:32.880 --> 07:34.350
You're not using your right leg?

07:34.350 --> 07:35.900
Or is it a feint?

07:36.860 --> 07:38.100
I've got it!

07:42.520 --> 07:44.340
Goal!

07:44.340 --> 07:45.620
It's 2-2!

07:45.620 --> 07:49.980
Germany pierces the Japanese defense to tie the game!

07:49.980 --> 07:52.070
Well done, Karl!

07:52.070 --> 07:53.900
Nice shot, brother!

07:56.900 --> 07:57.850
All right!

07:57.850 --> 08:00.100
Nice shot, Schneider!

08:00.100 --> 08:05.820
As the captain, I had no other option than to seize the opportunity you created.

08:05.820 --> 08:07.190
All right, let's do this!

08:07.190 --> 08:08.900
Let's keep up this pace and take the lead!

08:08.900 --> 08:10.420
Yeah!

08:18.440 --> 08:24.540
He made me hesitate for a moment because I know how good he is with his right foot.

08:24.540 --> 08:27.070
We're still tied, Wakabayashi-kun.

08:27.940 --> 08:30.430
The game's just starting.

08:30.940 --> 08:32.260
Tsubasa!

08:33.260 --> 08:36.220
Guys, the game will be decided with the next goal.

08:36.220 --> 08:39.380
We have to score at all costs to win this tournament!

08:39.380 --> 08:40.300
Yeah!

08:40.300 --> 08:43.980
That's it, Tsubasa. Cheer them up!

08:43.980 --> 08:47.220
The one who leads in the end takes the game!

08:47.220 --> 08:48.990
Don't give up before the game's over!

08:52.660 --> 08:54.810
The second half is nearing the end.

08:54.810 --> 08:59.940
Japan is holding their own against the powerful German team without any signs of giving up!

08:59.940 --> 09:03.760
Who would have been able to foresee this before the tournament?

09:03.760 --> 09:06.200
What superb inner strength Japan possesses!

09:07.900 --> 09:09.580
The game resumes.

09:09.580 --> 09:13.900
We'll win! We'll win to prove Germany's number one in the world!

09:13.900 --> 09:18.380
We won't lose after having come so far! We'll be the champions!

09:19.450 --> 09:21.440
There's only five minutes left.

09:21.440 --> 09:24.420
Will the winner be Japan or will it be Germany?

09:25.510 --> 09:27.700
Ohzora Tsubasa gets the ball.

09:27.700 --> 09:31.020
Let's go at it! Japan will score the final goal!

09:31.020 --> 09:33.180
All right, go for it, Tsubasa!

09:33.180 --> 09:34.700
I'll stop ya!

09:35.570 --> 09:38.860
The German midfielders hurry towards Tsubasa who has the ball.

09:38.860 --> 09:45.500
Japan's given us this much trouble because we let that Number 10 do whatever he wants!

09:47.560 --> 09:51.430
This time, we'll stop him with our pride as German midfielders!

09:51.430 --> 09:52.380
Let's do it!

09:56.060 --> 09:59.020
Sliding tackles. Ohzora dodges by jumping.

10:00.940 --> 10:02.980
There you are!

10:01.880 --> 10:02.980
Oh! Kartz jumps, too!

10:05.150 --> 10:07.740
Kartz stole the ball from Ohzora in midair!

10:08.380 --> 10:09.720
Good!

10:09.720 --> 10:14.620
The aggressive play by the German midfielders allowed them to take the ball from Ohzora!

10:15.520 --> 10:17.140
Well done! Let's do this!

10:22.660 --> 10:26.650
Oh, Ohzora, who was hit by Kartz, is not getting up,

10:26.650 --> 10:28.660
but the game still continues.

10:28.660 --> 10:30.100
Tsubasa!

10:31.220 --> 10:32.690
Tsubasa!

10:55.020 --> 10:57.460
Tsubasa!

10:59.200 --> 11:00.420
Get up, Tsubasa!

11:00.420 --> 11:03.020
Tsubasa!

11:01.310 --> 11:02.440
Tsubasa-san!

11:03.020 --> 11:03.820
Tsubasa-san!

11:03.820 --> 11:04.890
Tsubasa!

11:04.200 --> 11:04.890
Tsubasa!

11:04.890 --> 11:05.820
Tsubasa!

11:13.930 --> 11:17.620
Oh, Ohzora, who was hit by Kartz, is not getting up,

11:17.620 --> 11:19.100
but the game still continues.

11:19.100 --> 11:21.100
We'll be the ones who win this final!

11:21.100 --> 11:22.780
Keep up the pressure!

11:22.780 --> 11:24.220
Japan's in danger!

11:25.700 --> 11:27.020
Tsubasa...

11:27.020 --> 11:29.020
Tsubasa, hang on!

11:29.020 --> 11:30.570
Tsubasa-kun!

11:36.890 --> 11:38.020
Tsubasa-kun...

11:40.230 --> 11:41.430
Tsubasa-san!

11:44.300 --> 11:45.100
Tsubasa!

11:46.780 --> 11:47.860
Tsubasa-kun!

11:47.860 --> 11:49.840
Stand up, Tsubasa!

11:49.840 --> 11:53.820
You played all this time for the chance to score the winning goal, right?

11:53.820 --> 11:55.470
Stand up, Tsubasa!

11:55.470 --> 12:00.240
We have to win this game and show the world what Japanese soccer is all about!

12:01.980 --> 12:04.940
Stand up! I'm telling you to stand up!

12:05.590 --> 12:07.460
Stand up and score a goal!

12:07.460 --> 12:09.100
Tsubasa!

12:12.290 --> 12:16.400
Roberto... I can hear his voice.

12:17.080 --> 12:19.000
So you came to watch.

12:20.500 --> 12:22.020
Margas passes to the right side.

12:23.520 --> 12:25.060
Kartz attacks from the side.

12:25.060 --> 12:26.080
Come!

12:27.370 --> 12:29.720
You'll be the one to score the final goal.

12:29.720 --> 12:33.640
You, who will embody German... nope, European soccer,

12:33.640 --> 12:36.260
you, the Young German Emperor: Karl Heinz Schneider!

12:36.260 --> 12:38.060
The rest is up to you!

12:38.500 --> 12:39.440
All right!

12:39.440 --> 12:42.900
And now Schneider receives the pass right in front of the goal!

12:42.900 --> 12:44.380
Score, Karl!

12:44.380 --> 12:45.380
Brother!

12:49.380 --> 12:50.520
Stop him!

12:50.520 --> 12:52.260
Block him even if you die!

12:55.860 --> 12:56.460
It's no use!

12:58.380 --> 12:59.140
What?!

12:59.140 --> 13:02.540
Oh! Schneider lifts the ball over the defense!

13:02.540 --> 13:06.100
It's one-on-one between Schneider and Wakabayashi, and he prepares to shoot!

13:06.100 --> 13:08.180
All right, let's have this duel!

13:08.800 --> 13:11.510
You panicked, Wakabayashi. You went too early!

13:11.510 --> 13:13.180
The opposite side's mine!

13:18.180 --> 13:18.740
All right!

13:20.080 --> 13:21.220
Wakabayashi dives!

13:22.900 --> 13:23.780
Damn!

13:26.140 --> 13:27.580
He stopped it!

13:27.580 --> 13:29.750
Germany did not score the final goal!

13:29.750 --> 13:30.340
What?

13:30.340 --> 13:32.220
Wakabayashi!

13:32.940 --> 13:34.700
Do it, Tsubasa!

13:45.820 --> 13:46.780
Tsubasa!

13:49.940 --> 13:51.630
Tsubasa Ohzora finally stood up!

13:51.630 --> 13:52.820
The ball's for you, Tsubasa!

13:53.950 --> 13:55.290
That's right...

13:57.730 --> 13:59.060
I must score!

13:59.060 --> 14:01.330
We'll stop him again!

14:01.330 --> 14:02.780
We won't let you get a final chance!

14:02.780 --> 14:05.500
The German midfielders run towards Ohzora!

14:05.500 --> 14:06.980
Tsubasa-kun, over here!

14:06.980 --> 14:08.060
Misaki-kun!

14:09.500 --> 14:11.260
Stop him!

14:12.740 --> 14:14.540
Misaki dribbles forward!

14:15.860 --> 14:19.680
I'll make sure to properly give back the ball Tsubasa-kun entrusted to me!

14:19.680 --> 14:23.620
That's my job as part of the Golden Duo!

14:23.620 --> 14:24.620
Misaki attacks!

14:24.620 --> 14:26.380
I won't let you center the ball!

14:27.470 --> 14:29.340
Kojiro, I'm leaving this to you!

14:30.280 --> 14:32.780
Hyuga, the Japanese ace striker, is following up on the attack,

14:32.780 --> 14:35.540
but the German defenders are blocking his way!

14:35.540 --> 14:36.980
We have to stop him!

14:38.620 --> 14:40.020
Oh, he let it cross!

14:40.020 --> 14:42.650
We have to win the world title!

14:42.650 --> 14:44.460
I'm trusting you, Captain!

14:44.460 --> 14:47.380
The ball gets to Ohzora Tsubasa!

14:47.380 --> 14:48.540
Tsubasa!

14:47.380 --> 14:48.540
Tsubasa!

14:49.320 --> 14:50.540
No way!

14:52.270 --> 14:53.660
Schneider blocks!

14:56.870 --> 14:57.580
Not yet!

15:15.060 --> 15:16.180
Ohzora shoots!

15:18.300 --> 15:19.940
Müller can't reach it!

15:20.370 --> 15:21.540
It's the Drive Shot!

15:21.540 --> 15:23.080
But the ball's too high!

15:23.080 --> 15:24.100
Will it go in?

15:25.440 --> 15:26.380
Not yet!

15:29.900 --> 15:31.150
I will score!

15:31.150 --> 15:33.300
Ohzora does an overhead kick!

15:33.300 --> 15:33.900
I've got it!

15:40.810 --> 15:42.830
It's in!

15:46.120 --> 15:48.920
And that's the final whistle!

15:48.920 --> 15:51.940
The Japanese Junior Youth Team takes the world title!

15:53.030 --> 15:55.180
W-We did it!

15:55.180 --> 15:56.790
We won!

15:57.330 --> 15:58.650
We really won...

16:00.510 --> 16:02.000
We've got the victory.

16:02.000 --> 16:03.180
The victory...

16:03.610 --> 16:06.180
We did it! We're number one in the world!

16:07.670 --> 16:09.170
Guys!

16:09.170 --> 16:11.360
All right!

16:09.640 --> 16:11.340
Tsubasa!

16:11.360 --> 16:12.580
We really won!

16:12.580 --> 16:14.610
We did it!

16:14.610 --> 16:16.770
Tsubasa, we're the champions!

16:16.770 --> 16:18.330
We won!

16:18.330 --> 16:19.930
We're victorious!

16:20.970 --> 16:22.940
Japan's the winner!

16:22.940 --> 16:26.200
And this is Japan's first championship,

16:26.200 --> 16:30.970
in any international soccer tournament ever!

16:31.940 --> 16:34.410
Banzai!

16:34.410 --> 16:35.580
We did it!

16:35.580 --> 16:37.950
Congratulations, Tsubasa-kun!

16:40.940 --> 16:44.030
Honey, Tsubasa did it.

16:54.300 --> 16:56.610
We did it!

16:57.510 --> 16:59.410
We've got the victory!

17:02.900 --> 17:06.300
Congratulations, Japanese Junior Youth Team.

17:06.300 --> 17:07.980
Schneider!

17:11.270 --> 17:16.170
You really did great, Tsubasa Ohzora. You showed us a good game,

17:16.170 --> 17:19.140
but I'm sorry. I won't exchange uniforms.

17:20.650 --> 17:23.480
Our duel has only just begun.

17:23.480 --> 17:24.260
Yeah.

17:24.800 --> 17:25.720
The next time...

17:25.720 --> 17:27.820
It'll be at the International Cup.

17:27.820 --> 17:29.940
When that time comes, I won't lose.

17:29.940 --> 17:32.600
Yeah, we'll make sure to not lose either!

17:40.960 --> 17:45.180
Wakabayashi, we'll settle our score in the German League.

17:45.180 --> 17:46.660
Yes.

17:50.020 --> 17:52.050
Come on, guys.

17:52.050 --> 17:55.490
We gave it our all until the very end.

17:55.490 --> 17:58.800
Let's go out with our heads held high!

17:58.800 --> 18:00.020
Yeah!

18:00.020 --> 18:14.500
Japan! Japan! Japan!{I just added one of these, since I don't think we need to tell the audience that they keep saying "Japan!"}

18:06.460 --> 18:08.360
Thank you!

18:25.720 --> 18:26.750
We lost.

18:29.240 --> 18:30.410
Karl.

18:32.020 --> 18:34.560
You showed us a great game!

18:34.560 --> 18:39.060
I'm sorry I couldn't win when all of you came to watch.

18:39.930 --> 18:43.060
You gave it your all, and that's enough.

18:43.060 --> 18:45.860
And just like them, you're young.

18:46.420 --> 18:49.070
You'll play against each other numerous times.

18:49.070 --> 18:51.310
You can win the next time.

18:51.310 --> 18:52.180
Yes.

18:52.920 --> 18:53.860
Karl!

18:54.320 --> 18:59.860
By watching you, I understood what your father felt.

18:59.860 --> 19:01.260
Mother.

19:01.860 --> 19:03.720
It'll be fine.

19:03.720 --> 19:08.060
No matter what happens, 
I'll be by your father's side.

19:08.060 --> 19:09.420
Dear...

19:09.440 --> 19:14.380
I'm sorry for all of the trouble I've caused you all because I wasn't strong enough.

19:15.410 --> 19:17.750
Isn't that great, Brother?

19:17.750 --> 19:18.380
Yes!

19:18.810 --> 19:23.140
Family's just like soccer: 
you have to fight it through together!

19:23.140 --> 19:23.900
Yes!

19:24.470 --> 19:27.410
Mari, will you come watch me play another game?

19:27.410 --> 19:28.240
Yes!

19:32.540 --> 19:35.280
The Japanese players are running a victory lap around the pitch.

19:35.280 --> 19:38.100
They're saluting the public who's applauding them.

19:47.100 --> 19:50.720
You were right in the end, Roberto.

19:55.660 --> 19:58.420
Well done, Tsubasa!

19:58.420 --> 20:01.550
The way you play soccer is the soccer I love!

20:01.550 --> 20:04.650
I want to play soccer with you!

20:04.650 --> 20:06.820
I want to watch you become better at it!

20:08.800 --> 20:11.480
All right, everybody. Let's return.

20:11.480 --> 20:13.660
A party's waiting for you at the hotel.

20:13.660 --> 20:14.660
All right!

20:28.950 --> 20:31.740
R-Roberto!

20:32.670 --> 20:36.520
Well done, Tsubasa! Congratulations on winning the championship!

20:36.520 --> 20:39.170
So you <i>were </i>watching the game?

20:39.740 --> 20:41.120
Yeah.

20:41.120 --> 20:44.000
As a midfielder controlling the flow of the game {Timing:  I broke up one LONG line into three shorter lines so as to accommodate the pauses between the spoken dialogue.  Please adjust the timing of this line and the next two if needed.}

20:44.000 --> 20:46.600
and as a captain leading your teammates,

20:46.600 --> 20:48.740
you were truly formidable!

20:49.210 --> 20:50.660
Roberto...

20:52.740 --> 20:59.400
Let me help you in realizing your dream of becoming the world's best player.

20:59.400 --> 20:59.740
Eh?

20:59.740 --> 21:02.740
Come to Brazil, Tsubasa!

21:05.190 --> 21:06.940
Let's play soccer together!

21:13.960 --> 21:16.530
R-Roberto!

21:20.420 --> 21:22.330
I-I'll go!

21:22.330 --> 21:24.370
I'll go to Brazil and become a professional!

21:25.520 --> 21:28.460
Yeah, you can do it.

21:34.810 --> 21:36.240
Just as I thought.

21:43.470 --> 21:46.380
I've always believed

21:46.380 --> 21:53.460
that by becoming better at soccer, I'd be able to play with you again!

22:03.420 --> 22:09.340
